      Same three-card row, same long filename in the middle card. In "Broken" mode, watch
      it push the row wider than its container. In "Fixed" mode, the same card truncates
      its text with an ellipsis and the row stays put.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Only <code>min-width</code> differs between the two states — <code>flex-shrink</code>
      is identical in both. That's the point: shrink was always willing to act, it just had
      nowhere to go until the floor was removed.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      Open DevTools and inspect the middle card's computed <code>min-width</code> in each
      state: "auto" (resolving to the content's intrinsic width) vs. "0px" — the only
      change, and the entire difference in behavior.
    </p>
  </div>

